PE 808: Reversible Prime Squares / 可逆素数平方

=== Definition ===
Prime p where reverse(p^2) = q^2 for some prime q ≠ p.
Example: 13^2 = 169, reverse(169) = 961 = 31^2

=== Small examples ===
  13^2 = 169, reverse = 961 = 31^2 ✓
  31^2 = 961, reverse = 169 = 13^2 ✓

=== Known properties ===
Reversible prime squares come in pairs (p,q).
The first 50 such primes need to be summed.
